    "what_it_is": "10-epi-γ-Eudesmol is a sesquiterpenoid, a type of aromatic molecule that helps give certain essential oils their complex, earthy, and botanical scents. As a volatile compound, it easily evaporates into the air, which is why you might encounter it when crushing fragrant herbs or blending botanical perfumes.",
    "found_in": "It is found in the essential oils of several familiar aromatic plants, including clary sage (Salvia sclarea), sweet wormwood (Artemisia annua), and certain types of geranium and thyme.",
